Package: pathconverge
Type: Package
Title: Permutation Null Model for Cross-Omics Pathway Convergence
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: person("Chung-Hsien", "Lin", email = "author@example.org",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tests whether a nominated biomarker panel and a metabolic signature
    converge on shared biochemical pathways more often than expected under a
    size-matched permutation null. Pathway membership supports metabolite
    (KEGG compound) and gene modes; the convergence statistic supports binary
    co-membership and direction-aware scoring. Includes specificity-stratified
    convergence curves, a random-panel benchmark that randomises the
    panel-to-pathway mapping, and ORA-threshold sensitivity analyses.
    Developed and validated on an NSCLC plasma proteomics-metabolomics
    case study.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: data.table
Suggests: ggplot2, knitr, rmarkdown
VignetteBuilder: knitr
